 User preferences and request management remain available. Operational settings
 POST endpoints (including manual job triggers) are also disabled for now.
 
+## OIDC logout
+
+Each provider accepts `logoutMode`: `"local"` (the default) or `"provider"`.
+Provider mode destroys the Seerr session first, then the browser navigates to
+that provider's discovered `end_session_endpoint`. No tokens or automatic
+post-logout redirect parameters are sent, leaving the provider's logout choices
+visible (including Authentik's choice about ending the wider SSO session).
+Providers requiring an ID-token hint or other logout parameters are not supported.
+
+The authenticating provider is tracked in the server-side session, not inferred
+from linked accounts. Account linking does not change it. Existing sessions
+without this information log out locally; sign in again to enable provider
+logout. Local/Plex/Jellyfin logins always log out locally. Discovery failures,
+a missing endpoint, or a removed provider fall back to local logout; discovery
+has a three-second timeout. Local session destruction failures remain errors.
+This is browser-initiated logout, not back-channel or global session revocation.
+
 ## State and migration
 
